// @error is declared but has no implementation yet
// THE REMAINING HALF OF THE SPLIT: the STORE widths. The checker declares
// seventeen memory intrinsics; the emitter lowers twelve of them —
// `__store_i32__`, `__load_i32__`, `__log__`, the seven new load widths
// (`__load_i8__`/`__load_u8__`/`__load_i16__`/`__load_u16__`/`__load_i64__`/
// `__load_f32__`/`__load_f64__`), `__memory_size__` and `__memory_grow__`.
//
// The five with no emitter arm are `__store_i64__`, `__store_f32__` (this one),
// `__store_f64__`, `__store_string__` and `__log_string__` — re-censused at this
// head in three call POSITIONS each (statement / value / binding), which
// reproduces the count independently. They are deliberately outside the first
// slice: a program stores i32 words and reads them back at every width, which is
// what makes the load matrix measurable without also committing to a store
// surface. `docs/internals/buffer-design.md` §C2 has the full table and
// §"the smallest first slice" says why the stores wait.
//
// THE DIAGNOSTIC IS THE PART THAT MOVED. This file used to pin
// `@emit-error call to unknown function` — a message that reads like a typo'd
// IDENTIFIER when the identifier is real and the IMPLEMENTATION is what is
// missing, which `docs/internals/memory-gc-design.md` §1.2 filed as "the half
// worth fixing first". The checker now says so itself, positioned at the call,
// on the same unsupported-lowering channel `print` of a reference uses
// (`nameIsUnimplementedIntrinsic`).
//
// SHADOWING IS UNAFFECTED, and deliberately so: unlike the seven names #1167
// reserved, these five are not emitter-intercepted, so a program that DECLARES
// `function __store_f64__(…)` still shadows the builtin and still runs — the
// diagnostic is gated on `fnDeclIx` not holding the name.
__store_f32__(0, 1.5 as f32)
print(__load_i32__(0))
